<BaseLayout title="About the Project" description="Learn about WasmStore, an independent browser-game discovery library for classic games, community ports, source links, and practical play information." path="/about">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">PIXEL ARCADE · OUR STORY</div><h1>ABOUT THE <span class="gradient-text">PROJECT</span></h1><p>A clearer way to discover browser games, community-built ports, and the projects that keep classic play accessible on the web.</p></div></section>
  <article class="prose wrap legal-page">
    <p class="legal-kicker">WASMSTORE / PROJECT NOTES / 01</p>
    <h2>Welcome to WasmStore</h2>
    <p>WasmStore is an independent game-discovery directory built for people who enjoy classic games, browser experiments, and community-made web ports. It brings useful discovery information into one place: game descriptions, available demo links, source repositories, control notes, and practical context to help you decide what to try.</p>
    <p>The goal is straightforward: spend less time hunting through scattered links and more time understanding what a project is, where it comes from, and how to access it responsibly. WasmStore is a directory and guide—not a publisher, game studio, or official storefront for the titles listed here.</p>
    <h2>What you can find here</h2>
    <ul><li><strong>Game discovery:</strong> browse the catalog by platform or category and explore dedicated game pages.</li><li><strong>Demo and source links:</strong> where available, distinguish a playable demo from a project's source repository.</li><li><strong>Practical details:</strong> read available notes about controls, browser compatibility, input methods, and project requirements.</li><li><strong>Personal convenience:</strong> use browser-local features such as favorites where provided; these are designed to keep preferences on your own device.</li><li><strong>Helpful corrections:</strong> report broken links, outdated descriptions, accessibility problems, or attribution concerns.</li></ul>
    <h2>How listings are selected and described</h2>
    <p>Catalog entries are curated for discovery and may reference community-maintained catalogs, upstream repositories, project pages, and publicly available demos. A listing is not a technical certification. A link can become unavailable, a project can change its requirements, and a demo may not work in every browser or on every phone. We encourage visitors to check the linked project's own documentation and license before downloading, modifying, or redistributing anything.</p>
    <p>We aim to identify external destinations clearly and correct information when reliable details are brought to our attention. Inclusion does not imply that WasmStore has tested every feature, audited every file, or received permission to distribute a third-party project.</p>
    <h2>Ownership, licensing, and attribution</h2>
    <p>Game names, logos, characters, artwork, music, code, and other materials remain the property of their respective owners or licensors. Open-source and community projects remain subject to their own licenses. WasmStore does not claim ownership of third-party games and does not grant permission to copy or redistribute them. Please consult the original project's license and rights-holder information before reusing any material.</p>
    <p>If you believe a listing misrepresents a project or raises an intellectual-property concern, please read our <a href="/copyright">Copyright and Takedown Policy</a> and contact us with the relevant URLs and supporting details.</p>
    <h2>Independent by design</h2>
    <p>WasmStore is an unofficial, independent project. Unless a page clearly states otherwise, it is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or officially connected to the game developers, publishers, platforms, or trademark owners mentioned on the site. Read the full <a href="/non-affiliation">Non-Affiliation Notice</a> for details.</p>
    <h2>Accessibility and continuous improvement</h2>
    <p>We want the directory to remain readable and usable on desktop, tablet, and mobile screens. We aim for clear headings, meaningful links, keyboard-accessible controls, responsive layouts, and concise descriptions. Third-party games may have their own accessibility limitations that are outside our control. If something is difficult to use, tell us what device, browser, and page you were using so we can investigate.</p>
    <h2>Contact WasmStore</h2>
    <p>Have a suggestion, correction, game recommendation, or rights-related question? Visit the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>. For privacy details, see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>; for rules about using the directory, see our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
    <p class="legal-note"><strong>Editorial note:</strong> Catalog details and external links can change. We work to keep descriptions useful, but visitors should verify important technical, licensing, and availability details at the original source.</p>
  </article>
